## Visual concept used
A **calibration / benchmarking bench** rendered as a landscape left-to-right signal chain with a feedback return — the Part 5.0 sub-archetype within the locked "Engineering Diagnostic Instrument" style. Four inline stages carry the argument: **Stage 1 RAW INPUT** (a Hevy sample-stream block with a couple of visibly suspect rows), **Stage 2 QC GATE** (a calibration sieve drawn physically upstream of the benchmark, diverting five faulted samples — ego set, half-rep ROM, unit/typo, missing bodyweight, loaded-sled — into an amber `REJECTED` bin so the QC-before-benchmark ordering is unmissable), **Stage 3 BENCHMARK ENGINE** (the `AI · DIAGNOSTIC ENGINE` module with a two-tick reference ruler `NAT-ELITE`/`ENH-ELITE`, a "you" marker, and a green `WoW Δ gap closing` trend register), and the hero **Stage 4 OUTPUT READOUT** — a six-row benchmark gauge cluster (OHP→CURL→ROW→BENCH→HINGE→SQUAT) ranked worst-gap-first, each gauge showing the solid **gap-to-NAT** bar plus a hatched **extra-gap-to-ENH** segment with a per-lift RANK and RATING; the top row (OHP) is loudest, squat sits past NAT-ELITE. A green **feedback return rail** wraps full-width beneath the chain from the worst-ranked gauge back to the program input ("bias your weakest link next mesocycle", callback to Part 3.3's adaptation strip), closing the loop. Two **operator prompt cards** (ENTRY: full-body assessment · EXIT: program design) sit beneath, and a footer carries the 7-step order-of-operations guardrail, the "garbage in, confident garbage out" honesty line (amber), sources, and the series mark. Semantic color rationed to two states only — **success green** (WoW trend + feedback rail) and **warning amber** (QC rejects + the garbage-in line); danger/red deliberately unused, gauges kept in neutral chart-ink so the GAP, not hue, carries the read.

